          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observed, from their garden, two glowing red orbs, non-flashing, silent, slowly moving towards the East before disappearing. The observation of red orbs crossing a portion of the sky in just a few minutes, on a festive night, strongly suggests Thai lanterns, likely released nearby after a private party. The movement was observed towards the East, which is consistent with the North-West wind reported in Niort according to the weather record. The GEIPAN classified this case as \"B\", a probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
